  OWASP Dependency-Check False Positive Suppressions for VibeCheck

  HOW TO ADD A SUPPRESSION:
  1. Run the OWASP scan locally: mvn verify -P security-scan
  2. Open target/dependency-check-report.html
  3. For each false positive, find the CVE ID
  4. Add an entry below with the CVE ID and a note explaining why it's a false positive

  Format reference: https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!--
    Example suppression — REMOVE and add real ones as your scan finds false positives:

    <suppress>
      <notes>CVE-XXXX-YYYY affects library X only in context Y which VibeCheck does not use.</notes>
      <cve>CVE-XXXX-YYYY</cve>
    </suppress>
  -->

</suppressions>
